            <div xml:id="d334">

                <pb facs="0426" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">733.35/19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay (Wright) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-17T02:00:00-03:30">July 17, 1932—2
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. My 41, July 16, midnight. Presence here of two United States Coast Guard
                    vessels offers possible opportunity for conference on board between
                    representatives of both Governments. Bliss concurs in this suggestion. Please advise whether we may
                    be authorized to propose this to Uruguayan and Argentine Governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
